comments.body:
@jonasore mentioned that implementations should send over the direct send path (unencapsulated, or "naked"), in addition to the STUN paths. This seems reasonable (modulo the bandwidth concerns in #8) and resolves the concerns raised in the OP.

In spec text, this probably turns into something like

> Implementations MUST send handshake messages over the selected pair, once present, but MAY also transmit the same messages using STUN embedding.
